        "key": "D",
        "text": "8"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "9"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "D",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Exterior angles",
        "body": "Walking around a convex polygon you turn through $360°$ in total. At a $120°$ angle you turn $60°$, at a $150°$ angle $30°$. With $k$ angles of each kind: $k(60° + 30°) = 360°$, so $k = 4$ and the polygon has 8 angles.\n\n**Answer: (D) 8**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Angle sum",
        "body": "An $n$-gon has angle sum $(n - 2) \\cdot 180°$. With $n = 2k$: $k \\cdot 120° + k \\cdot 150° = (2k - 2) \\cdot 180°$, so $270k = 360k - 360$, $k = 4$, $n = 8$.\n\n**Answer: (D) 8**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
